# SurrealDB Architecture & Data Flow

This document outlines the database schema, involved tables, and end-to-end data flow for the Reengineering Budget Tracking tool. It serves as an engineering reference for the QA and implementation process.

---

## 1. Tables Involved in SurrealDB

The application interacts with several core tables inside the `project_budget` database (namespace `yerico`):

### A. `sites` (ReEngineering Progress & Work Orders)
* **Purpose**: This is the central transactional table. Each record represents one site-sector work order (ReEngineering progress).
* **Record ID Format**: `sites:<site_id>` (e.g., `sites:COC611`, `sites:TGR402`, etc.)
* **Fields Mapped & Synchronized**:
  * `site_id` (String) — Unique identifier for the base site.
  * `project_type` (String) — `COMBAT`, `FILTER`, `L2H`, `RESCOPING`, `BLACKSITE`.
  * `stage` (String) — Current step in the pipeline (e.g., `imported`, `permit`, `implementasi`, `atp`, `completed`).
  * `atp_number` / `po_id` / `sow_id` / `sector` (String/Number) — Work order parameters.
  * **Permit Fields**:
    * `permit_status` (String) — e.g. `5. Permit Released`
    * `permit_create_date` / `permit_start` / `permit_expiry` (Date Strings)
    * `pic` / `pic_telp` (String)
    * `tpas_no` / `tp_no` / `caf_no` (String)
    * `lock_type` (String)
  * **Implementation Fields**:
    * `implementasi_status` (String) — e.g. `RFS`
    * `team` (String) — Assigned execution team ID.
    * `field_leader_id` (String)
    * `plan_date` / `tanggal_rfs` / `ci_date` / `co_date` (Date Strings)
    * `impl_rfi_done` / `rfi_done` / `rfs_done` (Boolean)
  * `updated_at` / `initiated_at` (Datetime)

### B. `site_stage_logs` (Audit & History Logs)
* **Purpose**: Audit trails of all operational updates (field changes, stage transitions, files uploads).
* **Fields**:
  * `work_order_id` / `site_id` (String)
  * `action` (String) — e.g., `"Mengubah status permit menjadi 5. Permit Released"`
  * `user_id` (String)
  * `timestamp` (Datetime)

### C. `site_files` (Uploaded Documents & Evidence Photos)
* **Purpose**: Metadata of uploaded attachments (permit documents, RFI/RFS letters, site photos).
* **Fields**:
  * `work_order_id` / `site_id` (String)
  * `name` / `type` / `size` (String)
  * `category` (String) — `"document"` or `"photo"`
  * `uploaded_by` (String)
  * `timestamp` (Datetime)

---

## 2. End-to-End Data Flow

The following diagram visualizes the interactive data flow between the user interface, local memory states, and SurrealDB:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Field / Admin User
    participant FE as React Frontend UI State (localWo)
    participant Mock as Local Array State (atpWorkOrders)
    participant DB as SurrealDB (Production)

    Note over User, DB: Scenario A: Initial Page Load & Refresh
    DB->>Mock: SELECT * FROM sites (initAppDB on refresh)
    Note right of DB: Full permit & impl fields<br/>fetched and mapped
    Mock->>FE: Match by work order ID (setLocalWo)
    FE->>User: Displays latest synchronized data

    Note over User, DB: Scenario B: User edits a field (Auto-Save)
    User->>FE: Changes input field (e.g. PIC Nama)
    FE->>FE: setSaveStatus('saving')
    FE->>Mock: Update in-memory local copy (Object.assign)
    FE->>DB: UPDATE sites:<site_id> SET pic = $pic (via patchWO)
    DB-->>FE: Returns 200 OK
    FE->>FE: setSaveStatus('saved') (Success pop-up / toast)

    Note over User, DB: Scenario C: User updates stage & finishes process
    User->>FE: Clicks "Update Stage Permit"
    FE->>DB: UPDATE sites:<site_id> SET stage = 'implementasi'
    DB-->>FE: Returns 200 OK
    FE->>FE: showToastMsg('Sukses: Stage diperbarui!')
    Note over FE: Form transitions to locked default,<br/>"Perbarui Stage" & "Edit" buttons stay available
```

---

## 3. Core Architecture Rules & Best Practices Implemented

1. **Auto-Saving**: Input fields use `AutoSaveInput` components. When blurred or changed, they trigger `handleFieldSave`, which performs a delta update (`patchWO`) containing only the modified key.
2. **Key-Value Dictionary Mapping**: Frontend operational field names are mapped to SurrealDB database column names seamlessly:
   * `team_id` $\rightarrow$ `team`
   * `impl_status` $\rightarrow$ `implementasi_status`
   * `impl_notes` $\rightarrow$ `note_implementasi`
   * `actual_date` $\rightarrow$ `tanggal_rfs`
   * `tower_provider` $\rightarrow$ `tp_name`
3. **No-Loss-On-Refresh**: By ensuring `initAppDB` reads 100% of the active database columns and maps them directly into `atpWorkOrders` on launch, refreshes pull the exact state from your Production SurrealDB instantly.
